# The check after the field read only tests the typed array's class. The constant length at the allocation site is a claim by Link about the keyed read. The walk reads the array's own length,
# compares it with the claim, and stops where the claim is false. No element is read on the claim alone.
# The injected fault overstates the constant length of a typed array by one.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: undefined
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(FAULT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=OverstateTypedArrayLength
# FAULT: found an unexpected value in an element
# FAULT-NOT: went on
# FAULT: crashed
